    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the goblin confusion. Let's get straight to the point about flushing your water heater tank. Here's a simple step-by-step guide:\n\n1. Turn off the power to your water heater. This is usually done by switching off the circuit breaker that controls the heater.\n2. Turn off the cold water supply to the heater.\n3. Attach a garden hose to the drain valve at the bottom of the tank. Place the other end of the hose in a bucket or a drain to catch the water.\n4. Open the drain valve to let the water and sediment flow out.\n5. Once the water has stopped flowing, you can close the drain valve.\n6. Turn the power back on and then the cold water supply.\n7. Check the temperature of the water to see if it's now coming out hot.\n\nRemember, it's important to be patient and let the water and sediment completely drain out before you turn the power back on. If you're not comfortable with this process or if you encounter any issues, it's best to call a professional plumber. Safety first, and don't worry, there's no need for goblins in this situation!",
